   "type": "spec_point",
   "id": "spcpt_Bqr6RvC637zVPvBS",
   "name": "Logic Expressions",
   "definition": "\"(c) Write a logic expression from a:\n (i) problem statement\n (ii) logic circuit\n (iii) truth table\"\n"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Logic Expressions"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- A **logic expression** is a way of expressing a logic gate or logic circuit as an **equation**\n- The **output **appears on the **left **of the equals sign with the **inputs **and **logic gates** on the **right**"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "md": "| **Gate** | **Symbol** | **Truth Table** | **Logic Expression** |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **NOT** | ![not](assets/a35d1c8ac2f8-screenshot-2023-05-30-at-08-24-28.png) | \\| **A** \\| **Z** \\|<br>\\|---\\|---\\|<br>\\| 0 \\| 1 \\|<br>\\| 1 \\| 0 \\| | Z = NOT A |\n| **AND** | ![and](assets/28bda956492e-screenshot-2023-05-30-at-08-24-36.png) | \\| **A** \\| **B** \\| **Z** \\|<br>\\|---\\|---\\|---\\|<br>\\| 0 \\| 0 \\| 0 \\|<br>\\| 0 \\| 1 \\| 0 \\|<br>\\| 1 \\| 0 \\| 0 \\|<br>\\| 1 \\| 1 \\| 1 \\| | Z = A AND B |\n| **OR** | ![or](assets/46087ced0a82-screenshot-2023-05-30-at-08-24-49.png) | \\| **A** \\| **B** \\| **Z** \\|<br>\\|---\\|---\\|---\\|<br>\\| 0 \\| 0 \\| 0 \\|<br>\\| 0 \\| 1 \\| 1 \\|<br>\\| 1 \\| 0 \\| 1 \\|<br>\\| 1 \\| 1 \\| 1 \\| | Z = A OR B |\n| **NAND** | ![nand](assets/88cbded23e3f-screenshot-2023-05-30-at-08-25-01.png) | \\| **A** \\| **B** \\| **Z** \\|<br>\\|---\\|---\\|---\\|<br>\\| 0 \\| 0 \\| 1 \\|<br>\\| 0 \\| 1 \\| 1 \\|<br>\\| 1 \\| 0 \\| 1 \\|<br>\\| 1 \\| 1 \\| 0 \\| | Z = A NAND B |\n| **NOR** | ![nor](assets/dea8458c864e-screenshot-2023-05-30-at-08-25-22.png) | \\| **A** \\| **B** \\| **Z** \\|<br>\\|---\\|---\\|---\\|<br>\\| 0 \\| 0 \\| 1 \\|<br>\\| 0 \\| 1 \\| 0 \\|<br>\\| 1 \\| 0 \\| 0 \\|<br>\\| 1 \\| 1 \\| 0 \\| | Z = A NOR B |\n| **XOR** | ![xor](assets/9e0424c74965-screenshot-2023-05-30-at-08-25-28.png) | \\| **A** \\| **B** \\| **Z** \\|<br>\\|---\\|---\\|---\\|<br>\\| 0 \\| 0 \\| 0 \\|<br>\\| 0 \\| 1 \\| 1 \\|<br>\\| 1 \\| 0 \\| 1 \\|<br>\\| 1 \\| 1 \\| 0 \\| | Z = A XOR B |"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Logic circuits containing multiple gates can also be expressed as logic expressions/statements"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**An example logic circuit containing two inputs**"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2023/05/screenshot-2023-05-30-at-09-28-55.png",
   "file": "assets/7cd17a4e3c6a-screenshot-2023-05-30-at-09-28-55.png",
   "alt": "screenshot-2023-05-30-at-09-28-55",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- The logic circuit above can be expressed as the logic expression **Q= NOT(A OR B)**"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "** **"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**An example logic circuit containing two inputs**"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2023/05/screenshot-2023-05-30-at-09-29-06.png",
   "file": "assets/6ff4dde71d02-screenshot-2023-05-30-at-09-29-06.png",
   "alt": "screenshot-2023-05-30-at-09-29-06",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- The logic circuit above can be expressed as the logic expression **Q= (NOT A) AND B **"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**An example logic circuit containing three inputs**"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- The logic circuit above can be expressed as the logic expression **P = ((NOT A) OR B) NAND C**"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "** **"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**An example logic circuit containing three inputs**"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2023/05/screenshot-2023-05-30-at-09-35-30.png",
   "file": "assets/0f6f0c87413b-screenshot-2023-05-30-at-09-35-30.png",
   "alt": "screenshot-2023-05-30-at-09-35-30",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- This logic circuit above can be expressed as **X = NOT (A NAND B) OR (B NOR C)**"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "exam-tip",
   "label": "Exam Hint",
   "md": "- You may be required to write a logic expression/statement from a **truth table** or a **logic circuit**. You may also have to do the opposite - **draw a logic circuit** and **complete a truth table for a logic expression**"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "worked-example",
   "label": "Worked Example",
   "md": "Consider the logic statement: **X = (((A AND B) OR (C AND NOT B)) XOR NOT C) **\n\na. Draw a logic circuit to represent the given logic statement. **[6]**\n\n**Final answer:** **Answer**\n\n![screenshot-2023-05-30-at-09-37-21](assets/633425a0f395-screenshot-2023-05-30-at-09-37-21.png)\n\nOne mark per correct logic gate, with the correct input"
  }
 ]
